---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What this site collects, and what it does not.">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block: 2.5rem; max-width: 47rem;">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

    <div class="post-body">
      <p>
        {site.name} is a static content site. There is no sign-up, there are no accounts, and no
        form on it collects personal details.
      </p>

      <h2>What is not collected</h2>
      <p>
        We do not ask for or store your name, email address, phone number or any other identifying
        detail. There are no tracking cookies, no advertising pixels, and nothing is shared with
        third parties for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Accessibility preferences — text size, contrast and the rest — and your dark or light theme
        choice are kept in the browser's local storage. They stay on your device, are never sent to
        a server, and can be removed with the reset button in the accessibility menu or by clearing
        your browsing data.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The server that hosts the site records requests the way any web server does: IP address,
        time, the page requested and the browser type. Those logs are used for operating the site
        and diagnosing faults, nothing else. They are not cross-referenced with other sources and
        are not used to build a profile.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Fonts load from Google Fonts, so your browser contacts a Google server when a page loads,
        which exposes your IP address to Google under its own policy. Links inside posts lead to
        external sites — GitHub above all — and once you follow one, that site's privacy policy
        applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version appears on this page. There is no mailing list
        to announce it through, so a material change will also be flagged on the home page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Privacy questions go through the <a href="/about">about page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
